## State

- File: `loops/{{LOOP_SLUG}}.state.json` — runtime artifact, gitignored
  (`loops/*.state.json`): committed state would dirty the tree on every
  run. Missing file ⇒ the run initializes it (step 1).
- Shape: `{ "last_run": null, "processed": [], "consecutive_failures": 0 }`

## Trigger

- Primary: `{{ORCA_AUTOMATIONS_CREATE_COMMAND}}` (created `--disabled`;
  enabled only on the owner's explicit go)
- Manual fallback: "run one iteration of `loops/{{LOOP_SLUG}}.md`" to any
  agent — works with or without Orca
- Writes: report-only until the owner enables them

## Run protocol

1. Read the state file (missing ⇒ initialize with the shape above).
2. Precheck the queue: `{{QUEUE_COMMAND}}` — empty ⇒ stop.
3. Take at most {{MAX_ITEMS}} unprocessed items.
4. {{ACT_ON_ONE_ITEM}}; gate must exit 0 per item.
5. Update state (processed keys, `last_run`, failure count).
6. Stop per the stopping rule.
